[1.097,"o","\r                                   \u001b[1;4morbit\u001b[0m                                    \r\n\r\r\n\rA tiny service, here so the documentation's recordings have something to    \r\n\rpage through, pick from and search. Nothing in it runs.                     \r\n\r\r\n\r\u001b[4;35mWhat it does\u001b[0m                                                                \r\n\r\r\n\rorbit watches a queue, hands each job to a worker and reports progress in   \r\n\rthe terminal. Workers are plain functions; the scheduler decides how many   \r\n\rrun at once, retries a job that fails, and gives up after three tries.      \r\n\r\r\n\r\u001b[4;35mConfiguration\u001b[0m                                                               \r\n\r\r\n\r\u001b[36m                                                 \u001b[0m\r\n\r\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mSetting\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mDefault\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mMeaning\u001b[0m\u001b[1m                      \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\r\u001b[36m ─────────────────────────────────────────────── \u001b[0m\r\n\r\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mworkers\u001b[0m \u001b[36m \u001b[0m4       \u001b[36m \u001b[0mJobs that run at once        \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\r\u001b[2mlines 1–17 of 52 · ↑↓ PgUp PgDn · q quits\u001b[0m"]
